        }
      ],
      "id": "5ngz1j6"
    },
    {
      "id": "hu2b5uk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "1. Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zb70z3o",
      "content": "Metals are elements that tend to lose electrons and form positive ions (cations)."
    },
    {
      "id": "xvjn8uu",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "h7ofkoj",
      "src": "/books/Precis/RRB GS/images/image_h7ofkoj.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "4cldfq8",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "ljn26un",
      "src": "/books/Precis/RRB GS/images/image_ljn26un.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kzulgkd",
      "content": "They are generally hard, shiny, malleable and ductile."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3ztriwc",
      "content": "Most metals are good conductors of heat and electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9opuahr",
      "content": "Metals have high melting and boiling points (except sodium and potassium)."
    },
    {
      "id": "f5oww64",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Physical Properties of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3vu18o8",
      "content": "• Malleable – Can be beaten into sheets."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pd5abqa",
      "content": "• Ductile – Can be drawn into wires."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d5ujfd8",
      "content": "• Sonorous – Produce sound when struck."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p9600wt",
      "content": "• Lustrous – Shiny surface."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4p874kk",
      "content": "• Good conductors of heat and electricity."
    },
    {
      "id": "huvsi6b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2. Non-Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g91keq7",
      "content": "Non-metals gain electrons and form negative ions (anions)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "75rz1sc",
      "content": "They are generally soft and brittle."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "du25utc",
      "content": "Poor conductors of heat and electricity (except graphite)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m1pv5rw",
      "content": "Have low melting and boiling points."
    },
    {
      "id": "a1exu33",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Physical Properties of Non-Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9316jyj",
      "content": "• Brittle – Break easily."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yb5213j",
      "content": "• Non-sonorous."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1sm9eju",
      "content": "• Dull appearance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jwcglco",
      "content": "• Poor conductors."
    },
    {
      "id": "fp8znjr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3. Chemical Properties of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4jvqs1c",
      "content": "Metals react with oxygen to form metal oxides."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8nof2tm",
      "content": "Metal oxide + Water → Metal hydroxide (base)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bo2tpag",
      "content": "Metals react with acids to produce hydrogen gas."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xv47xy8",
      "content": "Metals react with water (some vigorously like Na, K)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t12rpbd",
      "content": "More reactive metal displaces less reactive metal from salt solution."
    },
    {
      "id": "ua71r3q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4. Chemical Properties of Non-Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Metals are electropositive elements that lose electrons to form cations.",
      "id": "ygvt195"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hcgc9bj",
      "content": "Non-metals react with oxygen to form acidic oxides."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8rix4kk",
      "content": "Non-metals generally do not react with acids."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h4fswwd",
      "content": "Non-metals form covalent bonds by sharing electrons."
    },
    {
      "id": "wi42pod",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5. Reactivity Series of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8ww8l6e",
      "content": "Metals arranged in decreasing order of reactivity:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5bw1aem",
      "content": "K &gt; Na &gt; Ca &gt; Mg &gt; Al &gt; Zn &gt; Fe &gt; Pb &gt; H &gt; Cu &gt; Hg &gt; Ag &gt; Au"
    },
    {
      "id": "k60hcnk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6. Corrosion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xydsnwp",
      "content": "Corrosion is the slow eating away of metals due to reaction with air and moisture."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pw1nr3u",
      "content": "Rusting is corrosion of iron forming Fe2O3·xH2O."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "09g3grt",
      "content": "Prevention methods: Painting, Galvanization, Alloying."
    },
    {
      "id": "0gndhdb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "7. Extraction of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xkipifm",
      "content": "Metals are extracted from ores."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "83r388h",
      "content": "Steps: Concentration → Roasting/Calcination → Reduction → Refining."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s4oxi7d",
      "content": "Highly reactive metals extracted by electrolysis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lbcp52x",
      "content": "Moderately reactive by reduction with carbon."
    },
